cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Drone traffic analytics for motorbike-heavy Vietnamese streets"
abstract: >
  Drone video pipeline for Ho Chi Minh City traffic built without hand annotation: pseudo-labelled
  YOLO11 students, active learning, TensorRT deployment, multi-object tracking and counting,
  click-to-lock target follow with a virtual gimbal, and traffic analytics (flight-log scale,
  speeds, turning movements, stopped and wrong-way events), each evaluated on frozen
  human-labelled test sets with bootstrap confidence intervals.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Baranenkov"
    given-names: "Vladislav"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NickHolden404/vn-drone-traffic"
license: AGPL-3.0
keywords:
  - "drone"
  - "UAV"
  - "traffic analytics"
  - "object detection"
  - "multi-object tracking"
  - "pseudo-labels"
  - "active learning"
